:Namespace test_SSE
⍝ Server-Sent Events (SSE) tests for Jarvis
⍝ Usage:
⍝   From the shell (repository root):  dyalogscript Tests/SSE/run.apls
⍝   From an APL session with #.Jarvis loaded:  #.test_SSE.Run
⍝ Run returns a vector of failure messages; empty means every test passed.
⍝ Each test starts its own Jarvis on its own port, and uses a raw Conga client (Jarvis's own LDRC, in Text mode)
⍝ so that the event stream can be read incrementally.
⍝ See Plans/sse.md, Phase 2, for the cases these tests cover.
⍝ Ports: every server in a run gets its own port, BasePort+1, BasePort+2, ... (8191 and up by default); ports are
⍝ never reused within a run, so one test's server can't receive another's traffic. If they clash with another
⍝ process, set BasePort before calling Run, or set the environment variable JARVIS_TEST_PORT for run.apls.

    (⎕IO ⎕ML)←1 1
    CRLF←⎕UCS 13 10
    LF←⎕UCS 10
    BOM←⎕UCS 65279
    BasePort←8190
    Verbose←1                ⍝ 1 = print each test's name and result as it runs

    TJarvisSource←':Class TJarvis: #.Jarvis' ':Field Public Logged←⍬' '∇ {msg}←{level}Log msg' ':Access public override' 'Logged,←⊂,⍕msg' '∇' ':EndClass'

    ∇ r←Run;tests;t;res
      :Access public
    ⍝ run every test_* function, returning a vector of failure messages
      r←⍬
      :If 9≠#.⎕NC'Jarvis'
          →0⊣r←,⊂'#.Jarvis is not loaded'
      :EndIf
      ⎕FIX TJarvisSource
      tests←{⍵/⍨'test_'∘≡¨5↑¨⍵}⎕NL ¯3
      PortsUsed←0
      :For t :In tests
          App←MakeApp
          (Servers Clients)←⍬ ⍬
          :Trap 0
              res←⍎t
          :Else
              res←,⊂'errored: ',⊃⎕DMX.DM
          :EndTrap
          StopAll
          r,←(⊂t,': '),¨res
          :If Verbose
              ⎕←t,': ',(1+0∊⍴res)⊃('FAILED (',(⍕≢res),')')'passed'
              ⎕←⍪res
          :EndIf
      :EndFor
    ∇

⍝ ─── the application code (CodeLocation) used by the tests ─────────────────────────

    ∇ app←MakeApp
      app←⎕NS''
      app.Reqs←⍬
      app.⎕FX'r←events req' 'Reqs,←req' 'r←0'
      app.⎕FX'r←alerts req' 'Reqs,←req' 'r←0'
      app.⎕FX'r←closer req' 'r←1'
      app.⎕FX'r←broken req' 'r←÷0'
      app.⎕FX'{r}←shy req' 'r←0'
      app.⎕FX'nores req' 'Reqs,←req'
      app.⎕FX'r←a dyadic b' 'r←0'
      app.a←⎕NS''
      app.a.⎕FX'r←b req' 'r←0'
      app.avar←42
      app.⎕FX'r←Authenticate req' 'r←~''secret''≡req.GetHeader''x-token'''
      app.⎕FX'r←CheckRequest req' 'r←''block''≡req.GetHeader''x-validate'''   ⍝ ValidateRequestFn: non-zero rejects
      app.⎕FX'r←AddLowerHeader req' '''x-app-header''req.SetHeader''1''' 'r←0'  ⍝ ValidateRequestFn: adds a lower-case header
      app.PostCalled←0
      app.⎕FX'AfterRequest req' 'PostCalled+←1'                                ⍝ PostProcessFn
      app.⎕FX'r←echo payload' 'r←payload'                                       ⍝ an ordinary JSON endpoint
      app.(LoopTid LoopDone)←0 0
      app.⎕FX'r←killme req;i' 'req.KillOnDisconnect←1' 'LoopTid←⎕TID' ':For i :In ⍳100' '⎕DL 0.1' ':EndFor' 'r←0'
      app.⎕FX'r←looper req;i;rc' 'LoopTid←⎕TID' ':For i :In ⍳100' '⎕DL 0.1' 'rc←req req.Server.SendSSE''tick''' ':If 0≠⊃rc' ':Leave' ':EndIf' ':EndFor' 'LoopDone←1' 'r←0'
    ∇

⍝ ─── helpers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Expect←{⍺:0⍴⊂'' ⋄ ,⊂⍵}                 ⍝ cond Expect 'message'  →  ⍬ if cond, else the message
    Show←{∊{⍵=LF:'<LF>' ⋄ ⍵=⎕UCS 13:'<CR>' ⋄ ⍵}¨,⍕⍵}   ⍝ make line breaks visible in messages
    Contains←{∨/⍺⍷⍵}                        ⍝ 'needle' Contains 'haystack'
    LoggedMatch←{∨/∨/¨(⊂⍵)⍷¨⍺.Logged}       ⍝ j LoggedMatch 'text'

    ∇ j←NewServer endpoints
    ⍝ create (but don't start) a test server on its own port
      j←⎕NEW TJarvis
      j.Port←BasePort+PortsUsed←PortsUsed+1
      j.CodeLocation←App
      j.SSEEndpoints←endpoints
      j.DYALOG_JARVIS_THREAD←'debug'
      j.SSEHeartbeatInterval←0
      j.WaitTimeout←5000 ⍝ Stop allows the server this long to finish
      Servers,←j
    ∇

    ∇ StopAll;j;c
    ⍝ stop every server this test started and close its clients
      :For j :In Servers
          :Trap 0
              {}j.Stop
              {}j.LDRC.Close j.ServerName ⍝ in case the server was Reset rather than stopped
          :EndTrap
      :EndFor
      :For c :In Clients
          :Trap 0 ⋄ {}#.Jarvis.LDRC.Close c ⋄ :EndTrap
      :EndFor
      (Servers Clients)←⍬ ⍬
    ∇

    ∇ c←j Connect path
    ⍝ open a raw client to server j and send a GET for path with an SSE Accept header
      c←j Request('GET'path(,⊂'Accept' 'text/event-stream'))
    ∇

    ∇ c←j Request args;method;path;headers;body;version;req
    ⍝ open a raw client to server j and send one HTTP request; c is the client name
    ⍝ args: method path headers [body [version]]; headers is a vector of (name value) pairs
      (method path headers body version)←5↑args,(≢args)↓'' '' ⍬ '' 'HTTP/1.1'
      req←method,' ',path,' ',version,CRLF,'Host: localhost',CRLF
      req,←∊{⍺,': ',⍵,CRLF}/¨headers
      req,←(method≢'GET')/'Content-Length: ',(⍕≢body),CRLF
      req,←CRLF,body
      c←j SendRaw req
    ∇

    ∇ c←j SendRaw text;rc
    ⍝ open a raw client to server j and send text; c is the client name
      (rc c)←2↑j.LDRC.Clt'' 'localhost'j.Port'Text'
      'Could not connect'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨rc≠0
      Clients,←⊂c
      {}j.LDRC.Send c text
    ∇

    ∇ r←j Echo headers
    ⍝ make an ordinary (non-SSE) JSON request to /echo and read its response headers; r is the client name
      r←j Request('POST' '/echo'((⊂'Content-Type' 'application/json'),headers)'{}')
    ∇

    ∇ r←WaitFor(cond ms);end
    ⍝ evaluate the expression cond every 100ms, for up to ms milliseconds; r is 1 as soon as it's true
      end←ms+⎕AI[3]
      :Repeat
          :If ⍎cond ⋄ →0⊣r←1 ⋄ :EndIf
          {}⎕DL 0.1
      :Until ⎕AI[3]>end
      r←⍎cond
    ∇

    ∇ (data closed)←j Read(c until ms);end;res;rc;evt
    ⍝ read from client c until the text "until" has been received (or, if until is 1, until the data ends with a
    ⍝ blank line), the connection closes, or ms milliseconds have passed
      data←'' ⋄ closed←0 ⋄ end←ms+⎕AI[3]
      :While ⎕AI[3]<end
          res←j.LDRC.Wait c 100
          (rc evt)←(4↑res,4⍴⊂'')[1 3]
          :If rc=0
              :If (⊂evt)∊'Block' 'BlockLast'
                  data,←4⊃res
              :EndIf
              :If (⊂evt)∊'BlockLast' 'Closed' 'Error'
                  closed←1 ⋄ :Leave
              :EndIf
          :ElseIf rc≠100 ⍝ 100 = timeout; anything else (e.g. 1010 object not found) means the connection is gone
              closed←1 ⋄ :Leave
          :EndIf
          :If until≡1
              :If LF LF≡¯2↑data ⋄ :Leave ⋄ :EndIf
          :ElseIf ~0∊⍴until
              :If until Contains data ⋄ :Leave ⋄ :EndIf
          :EndIf
      :EndWhile
    ∇

    ∇ (status headers body)←ParseResponse data;i;head;lines
    ⍝ split a raw HTTP response into status code, header matrix (lower-case names) and body
      status←0 ⋄ headers←0 2⍴⊂'' ⋄ body←''
      →0⍴⍨0∊⍴i←⍸(CRLF,CRLF)⍷data
      head←(¯1+⊃i)↑data
      body←(3+⊃i)↓data
      lines←{⍵~⎕UCS 13}¨(head≠⎕UCS 10)⊆head
      status←⊃(//)⎕VFI 2⊃' '(≠⊆⊢)⊃lines
      headers←↑{i←⍵⍳':' ⋄ (⎕C(i-1)↑⍵)({⍵↓⍨+/∧\' '=⍵}i↓⍵)}¨1↓lines
    ∇

    ∇ r←headers Header name
      r←(headers[;1]⍳⊂⎕C name)⊃headers[;2],⊂''
    ∇

    ∇ (status headers body closed)←j Open path;data
    ⍝ connect to an SSE endpoint and read the response headers and the initial ": connected" comment
    ⍝ the client's name is left in Last, and the raw text received in LastRaw, for the caller's later use
      Last←j Connect path
      (data closed)←j Read Last(': connected',LF,LF)3000
      LastRaw←data
      (status headers body)←ParseResponse data
    ∇

    ∇ r←WaitGone(j conx);end
    ⍝ wait up to 3 seconds for conx to disappear from j.SSEConnections''; r is 1 if it did
      end←3000+⎕AI[3]
      :Repeat
          :If ~(⊂conx)∊j.SSEConnections''
              →0⊣r←1
          :EndIf
          {}⎕DL 0.1
      :Until ⎕AI[3]>end
      r←0
    ∇

⍝ ─── tests ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←test_Startup;j;rc;msg;status;headers;body;closed
    ⍝ start-up checks of SSEEndpoints and the endpoint functions (plan §2.1, §4.7)
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events nofn'
      (rc msg)←j.Start
      r,←(rc=0)Expect'Start with a function and a missing function failed: ',⍕msg
      :If rc=0 ⍝ an endpoint with no function still streams
          (status headers body closed)←j Open'/nofn'
          r,←((status=200)∧~closed)Expect'GET /nofn (no endpoint function): status ',(⍕status),(closed/', stream closed')
          r,←(1=≢j.SSEConnections'nofn')Expect'GET /nofn: SSEConnections ''nofn'' should list 1 connection'
      :EndIf
      {}j.Stop

      j←NewServer'shy nores events'
      (rc msg)←j.Start
      r,←(rc=0)Expect'shy, no-result and explicit-result endpoint functions should be accepted: ',⍕msg
      {}j.Stop

      j←NewServer'dyadic'
      (rc msg)←j.Start
      r,←(rc≠0)Expect'a dyadic endpoint function should be rejected'
      r,←('is not a'Contains⍕msg)Expect'dyadic rejection message is not readable: ',⍕msg

      j←NewServer'avar'
      (rc msg)←j.Start
      r,←(rc≠0)Expect'a variable with an endpoint''s name should make Start fail (§4.7)'
      r,←('avar'Contains⍕msg)Expect'the Start failure message should name the variable: ',⍕msg
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Shutdown;j;t;res
    ⍝ Start then Stop returns promptly, with and without SSE endpoints
      r←⍬
      :For j :In (NewServer'')(NewServer'events')
          :If 0≠⊃res←j.Start
              r,←⊂'Start failed: ',⍕res ⋄ :Continue
          :EndIf
          t←⎕AI[3]
          res←j.Stop
          r,←(res≡0 'Server stopped')Expect'Stop returned ',⍕res
          r,←(5000>⎕AI[3]-t)Expect'Stop took ',(⍕⎕AI[3]-t),'ms'
      :EndFor
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Handshake;j;status;headers;body;closed;head
    ⍝ GET returns 200, the SSE headers, and a ": connected" comment
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events'
      j.ValidateRequestFn←'AddLowerHeader' ⍝ adds a lower-case header, to check that header names are capitalised
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (status headers body closed)←j Open'/events'
      r,←(status=200)Expect'status ',(⍕status),', expected 200; body: ',Show body
      r,←('text/event-stream; charset=utf-8'≡headers Header'content-type')Expect'content-type: ',headers Header'content-type'
      r,←('no-cache'≡headers Header'cache-control')Expect'cache-control: ',headers Header'cache-control'
      r,←('no'≡headers Header'x-accel-buffering')Expect'x-accel-buffering: ',headers Header'x-accel-buffering'
      r,←((': connected',LF,LF)≡body)Expect'body should be ": connected" + blank line, got: ',Show body
      r,←(~closed)Expect'stream closed unexpectedly'
      r,←(1=≢j.SSEConnections'events')Expect'SSEConnections ''events'' should list 1 connection'
      head←LastRaw↑⍨¯1+⊃(⍸(CRLF,CRLF)⍷LastRaw),≢LastRaw
      r,←(('X-App-Header: 1'Contains head)∧'Content-Type: text/event-stream'Contains head)Expect'raw header names should be capitalised (x-app-header → X-App-Header); got: ',Show head
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Rejections;j;c;status;headers;body;data;closed
    ⍝ wrong method, unacceptable Accept header, no Accept header, CORS, authentication
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'

      c←j Request('POST' '/events'⍬)
      (status headers body)←ParseResponse⊃j Read c(CRLF,CRLF)3000
      r,←(status=405)Expect'POST: status ',(⍕status),', expected 405'

      c←j Request('GET' '/events'(,⊂'Accept' 'application/json'))
      (status headers body)←ParseResponse⊃j Read c(CRLF,CRLF)3000
      r,←(status=406)Expect'Accept: application/json: status ',(⍕status),', expected 406'

      c←j Request('GET' '/events'⍬)
      (status headers body)←ParseResponse⊃j Read c(': connected',LF,LF)3000
      r,←(status=200)Expect'no Accept header: status ',(⍕status),', expected 200'

      c←j Request('OPTIONS' '/events'(('Origin' 'http://example.com')('Access-Control-Request-Method' 'GET')))
      (status headers body)←ParseResponse⊃j Read c(CRLF,CRLF)3000
      r,←(status=204)Expect'CORS preflight: status ',(⍕status),', expected 204'
      r,←(~0∊⍴headers Header'access-control-allow-origin')Expect'CORS preflight: no Access-Control-Allow-Origin header'

      c←j Request('GET' '/events'(('Origin' 'http://example.com')('Accept' 'text/event-stream')))
      (status headers body)←ParseResponse⊃j Read c(': connected',LF,LF)3000
      r,←(status=200)Expect'CORS GET: status ',(⍕status),', expected 200'
      r,←((,'*')≡headers Header'access-control-allow-origin')Expect'CORS GET: Access-Control-Allow-Origin is "',(headers Header'access-control-allow-origin'),'"'
      {}j.Stop

      j←NewServer'events'
      j.AuthenticateFn←'Authenticate'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start with AuthenticateFn failed'
      c←j Connect'/events'
      (data closed)←j Read c(CRLF,CRLF)3000
      (status headers body)←ParseResponse data
      r,←(status=401)Expect'no credentials: status ',(⍕status),', expected 401'
      r,←(~'event-stream'Contains headers Header'content-type')Expect'authentication failure should not start a stream'
      c←j Request('GET' '/events'(('Accept' 'text/event-stream')('x-token' 'secret')))
      (status headers body)←ParseResponse⊃j Read c(': connected',LF,LF)3000
      r,←(status=200)Expect'valid credentials: status ',(⍕status),', expected 200'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_EndpointNames;cases;case;setting;paths;path;j;status;headers;body;closed
    ⍝ every accepted form of SSEEndpoints routes to the right endpoints (normalizeEndpoint)
      r←⍬
      cases←⍬
      cases,←⊂'events'(,⊂'/events')
      cases,←⊂'/events'(,⊂'/events')
      cases,←⊂'a.b'(,⊂'/a/b')
      cases,←⊂'/a/b'(,⊂'/a/b')
      cases,←⊂'/events, a/b'('/events' '/a/b')
      cases,←⊂('/events' 'a/b')('/events' '/a/b')
      :For (setting paths) :In cases
          j←NewServer setting
          :If 0≠⊃j.Start
              r,←⊂'SSEEndpoints←',(Show setting),': Start failed' ⋄ :Continue
          :EndIf
          :For path :In paths
              (status headers body closed)←j Open path
              r,←((status=200)∧'event-stream'Contains headers Header'content-type')Expect'SSEEndpoints←',(Show setting),': GET ',path,' gave status ',⍕status
          :EndFor
          {}j.Stop
      :EndFor
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_EndpointFunction;j;status;headers;body;closed;data
    ⍝ result 0 keeps the stream open, non-zero closes it, an error closes it and is logged
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events closer broken'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'

      (status headers body closed)←j Open'/events'
      (data closed)←j Read Last''1500
      r,←(~closed)Expect'events (result 0): stream should stay open'
      r,←(1=≢App.Reqs)Expect'events: the endpoint function should have been called once'
      :If 1=≢App.Reqs
          r,←(1≡(⊃App.Reqs).IsSSE)Expect'events: req.IsSSE should be 1'
          r,←((⊃App.Reqs).Connection≡⊃j.SSEConnections'events')Expect'events: req.Connection should match SSEConnections: ',(⊃App.Reqs).Connection
      :EndIf

      (status headers body closed)←j Open'/closer'
      :If ~closed ⋄ (data closed)←j Read Last''3000 ⋄ :EndIf
      r,←closed Expect'closer (result 1): stream should be closed'

      (status headers body closed)←j Open'/broken'
      :If ~closed ⋄ (data closed)←j Read Last''3000 ⋄ :EndIf
      r,←closed Expect'broken (error): stream should be closed'
      r,←(j LoggedMatch'Error in SSE handler for endpoint broken')Expect'broken: the error should be logged'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Sending;j;c1;c2;n1;n2;data;closed;res
    ⍝ SendSSE by connection name and by Request; broadcasts via SSEConnections
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events alerts'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      {}j Open'/events' ⋄ c1←Last
      {}j Open'/alerts' ⋄ c2←Last
      n1←j.SSEConnections'events'
      n2←j.SSEConnections'/alerts'
      r,←(1 1≡≢¨n1 n2)Expect'SSEConnections should list one connection per endpoint, got ',⍕≢¨n1 n2
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r

      res←n1 j.SendSSE'by name'
      (data closed)←j Read c1 1 2000
      r,←(('data: by name',LF,LF)≡data)Expect'send by name: got ',Show data
      r,←(res≡,0)Expect'send by name: result ',⍕res

      res←(⊃App.Reqs)j.SendSSE'by request'
      (data closed)←j Read c1 1 2000
      r,←(('data: by request',LF,LF)≡data)Expect'send by Request: got ',Show data

      res←(j.SSEConnections'')j.SendSSE'everyone'
      r,←(res≡0 0)Expect'broadcast to all: result ',⍕res
      r,←(('data: everyone',LF,LF)≡⊃j Read c1 1 2000)Expect'broadcast to all: events client did not receive it'
      r,←(('data: everyone',LF,LF)≡⊃j Read c2 1 2000)Expect'broadcast to all: alerts client did not receive it'

      {}(j.SSEConnections'alerts')j.SendSSE'alerts only'
      r,←(('data: alerts only',LF,LF)≡⊃j Read c2 1 2000)Expect'per-endpoint broadcast: alerts client did not receive it'
      r,←(0∊⍴⊃j Read c1 1 700)Expect'per-endpoint broadcast: events client should not receive it'

      r,←(2=≢j.SSEConnections'events, /alerts')Expect'SSEConnections with two endpoints should list 2 connections'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Payloads;j;c;conx;cases;what;expected;data;closed;ns
    ⍝ what SendSSE actually puts on the wire for each kind of payload (plan §4.2)
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      {}j Open'/events' ⋄ c←Last
      conx←j.SSEConnections'events'
      ns←⎕NS'' ⋄ ns.a←1
      cases←⍬
      cases,←⊂('event: e',LF,'data: x',LF,LF)('event: e',LF,'data: x',LF,LF)   ⍝ pre-formatted: byte for byte
      cases,←⊂'hello'('data: hello',LF,LF)
      cases,←⊂('l1' 'l2')('data: l1',LF,'data: l2',LF,LF)
      cases,←⊂(2 2⍴'abcd')('data: ab',LF,'data: cd',LF,LF)
      cases,←⊂(BOM,'data: x',LF,LF)('data: x',LF,LF)                          ⍝ BOM stripped
      cases,←⊂''(':',LF,LF)                                                    ⍝ empty → keep-alive comment
      cases,←⊂BOM(':',LF,LF)                                                   ⍝ lone BOM → keep-alive comment
      cases,←⊂42('data: 42',LF,LF)                                             ⍝ plan §3 item 1
      cases,←⊂ns('data: {"a":1}',LF,LF)                                        ⍝ plan §3 item 1
      cases,←⊂(1 2 3)('data: [1,2,3]',LF,LF)
      cases,←⊂'a'('data: a',LF,LF)                                             ⍝ character scalar, plan §3 item 2
      :For (what expected) :In cases
          {}conx j.SendSSE what
          (data closed)←j Read c 1 2000
          r,←(expected≡data)Expect'payload ',(Show what),': expected ',(Show expected),', got ',Show data
          :If closed ⋄ r,←⊂'stream closed after payload ',Show what ⋄ :Leave ⋄ :EndIf
      :EndFor
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_NonSSETarget;j;res
    ⍝ SendSSE to a connection that isn't an open SSE connection returns ¯1, sends nothing, and logs it
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      res←'CON99999999'j.SendSSE'nobody'
      r,←(res≡,¯1)Expect'SendSSE to an unknown connection returned ',⍕res
      r,←(j LoggedMatch'non-SSE or closed connection')Expect'SendSSE to an unknown connection was not logged'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Disconnect;j;conx;res
    ⍝ closing the client removes the connection, and a later SendSSE to it fails
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      {}j Open'/events'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(1=≢j.SSEConnections'events')Expect'no SSE connection was opened'
      conx←⊃j.SSEConnections'events'
      {}j.LDRC.Close Last
      r,←(WaitGone j conx)Expect'connection ',conx,' still listed 3s after the client closed'
      res←conx j.SendSSE'too late'
      r,←(0≠⊃res)Expect'SendSSE to a closed connection returned 0'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Heartbeat;j;data;closed;t;d;n;interval
    ⍝ heartbeat comments arrive at the configured interval, and not at all when it's 0
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events'
      j.SSEHeartbeatInterval←1
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      {}j Open'/events'
      (data closed)←j Read Last(':',LF,LF)3000
      r,←((':',LF,LF)≡data)Expect'SSEHeartbeatInterval←1: no heartbeat within 3s, got ',Show data
      t←⎕AI[3]
      {}j.Stop
      r,←(5000>⎕AI[3]-t)Expect'Stop with the heartbeat running took ',(⍕⎕AI[3]-t),'ms'

      j←NewServer'events'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start (interval 0) failed'
      {}j Open'/events'
      (data closed)←j Read Last''2500
      r,←(0∊⍴data)Expect'SSEHeartbeatInterval←0: unexpected data ',Show data

      r,←(30≡(⎕NEW TJarvis).SSEHeartbeatInterval)Expect'SSEHeartbeatInterval should default to 30'

    ⍝ interval 0 must start no heartbeat thread (no data in 2.5s alone can't tell 0 from 30)
      d←⍬
      :For interval :In 0 1
          j←NewServer'events'
          j.SSEHeartbeatInterval←interval
          n←≢⎕TNUMS
          →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start (interval ',(⍕interval),') failed'
          {}⎕DL 0.5
          d,←(≢⎕TNUMS)-n
      :EndFor
      r,←((1+⊃d)=2⊃d)Expect'interval 1 should start exactly one more thread than interval 0; threads started: ',⍕d
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Timeouts;j;data;closed;conx;c;status;headers;body;sse
    ⍝ an SSE connection is not closed by ConnectionTimeout, while an idle ordinary connection is (the control)
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events'
      j.(ConnectionTimeout WaitTimeout)←1 200
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      {}j Open'/events' ⋄ sse←Last
      c←j Echo ⍬
      (status headers body)←ParseResponse⊃j Read c'{}' 3000
      r,←(status=200)Expect'control: POST /echo gave status ',⍕status
      (data closed)←j Read sse''3000
      r,←(~closed)Expect'the SSE stream was closed within 3s with ConnectionTimeout←1'
      (data closed)←j Read c''1000
      r,←closed Expect'control: an idle keep-alive connection should be closed by ConnectionTimeout←1, so cleanup never ran'
      Last←sse
      conx←j.SSEConnections'events'
      {}conx j.SendSSE'still here'
      (data closed)←j Read Last 1 2000
      r,←(('data: still here',LF,LF)≡data)Expect'no event received after ConnectionTimeout had passed: ',Show data
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_BeforeAfter;j
    ⍝ SSEConnections returns '' before Start, after Stop and after Reset
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events'
      r,←(0∊⍴j.SSEConnections'')Expect'before Start: SSEConnections should be empty'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      {}j Open'/events'
      r,←(1=≢j.SSEConnections'')Expect'while running: SSEConnections should list 1 connection'
      {}j.Stop
      r,←(0∊⍴j.SSEConnections'')Expect'after Stop: SSEConnections should be empty'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'restart failed'
      {}j Open'/events'
      {}j.Reset
      r,←(0∊⍴j.SSEConnections'')Expect'after Reset: SSEConnections should be empty'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_FormatSSE;J;cases;args;expected;got;ns
    ⍝ unit cases for the public shared FormatSSE
      r←⍬
      J←#.Jarvis
      cases←⍬
      cases,←⊂(⊂'hello')('data: hello',LF,LF)
      cases,←⊂(⊂'a',(⎕UCS 13 10),'b',(⎕UCS 13),'c')('data: a',LF,'data: b',LF,'data: c',LF,LF)
      cases,←⊂(⊂2 2⍴'abcd')('data: ab',LF,'data: cd',LF,LF)
      cases,←⊂(⊂'xx' 'yy')('data: xx',LF,'data: yy',LF,LF)
      cases,←⊂(⊂1 2 3)('data: [1,2,3]',LF,LF)
      cases,←⊂(⊂'')(':',LF,LF)
      cases,←⊂(⊂'a')('data: a',LF,LF)                                                   ⍝ plan §3 item 2
      cases,←⊂('ping' 'x')('event: ping',LF,'data: x',LF,LF)
      cases,←⊂(('update' '42' '3000')'x')('event: update',LF,'id: 42',LF,'retry: 3000',LF,'data: x',LF,LF)
      cases,←⊂(('update' '' 'soon')'x')('event: update',LF,'data: x',LF,LF)             ⍝ empty id and bad retry omitted
      cases,←⊂(('e',LF,'vil')'x')('event: evil',LF,'data: x',LF,LF)                     ⍝ line breaks stripped from fields
      :For (args expected) :In cases
          got←{1=≢⍵:J.FormatSSE⊃⍵ ⋄ (⊃⍵)J.FormatSSE 2⊃⍵}args
          r,←(expected≡got)Expect'FormatSSE ',(Show args),': expected ',(Show expected),', got ',Show got
      :EndFor
      ns←⎕NS'' ⋄ ns.(event id retry)←'upd' 7 250
      got←ns J.FormatSSE'x'
      r,←(('event: upd',LF,'id: 7',LF,'retry: 250',LF,'data: x',LF,LF)≡got)Expect'FormatSSE with namespace fields: got ',Show got
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_IsSSEText;J;cases;s;expected
    ⍝ unit cases for the public shared IsSSEText
      r←⍬
      J←#.Jarvis
      cases←⍬
      cases,←⊂('data: x',LF,LF)1
      cases,←⊂('data: x',CRLF,CRLF)1
      cases,←⊂('data: x',LF)0                        ⍝ unterminated
      cases,←⊂'hello' 0
      cases,←⊂(':',LF,LF)1                           ⍝ comment
      cases,←⊂('foo: x',LF,LF)0                      ⍝ unknown field → wrapped (by design)
      cases,←⊂('retry: soon',LF,LF)0
      cases,←⊂42 0
      cases,←⊂(⊂'data: x')0
      cases,←⊂('data: a',LF,LF,'event: e',LF,'data: b',LF,LF)1
      :For (s expected) :In cases
          r,←(expected≡J.IsSSEText s)Expect'IsSSEText ',(Show s),' should be ',⍕expected
      :EndFor
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_REST;j;status;headers;body;closed;data
    ⍝ SSE works in REST mode too (plan §1)
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events'
      j.Paradigm←'REST'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start in REST mode failed'
      (status headers body closed)←j Open'/events'
      r,←((status=200)∧'event-stream'Contains headers Header'content-type')Expect'REST: GET /events gave status ',⍕status
      {}(j.SSEConnections'events')j.SendSSE'rest'
      (data closed)←j Read Last 1 2000
      r,←(('data: rest',LF,LF)≡data)Expect'REST: event not received: ',Show data
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Validate;j;c;status;headers;body;closed
    ⍝ ValidateRequestFn applies to SSE requests (plan §4.6)
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events'
      j.ValidateRequestFn←'CheckRequest'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start with ValidateRequestFn failed'
      c←j Request('GET' '/events'(('Accept' 'text/event-stream')('x-validate' 'block')))
      (status headers body)←ParseResponse⊃j Read c(CRLF,CRLF)3000
      r,←(status=400)Expect'rejected by ValidateRequestFn: status ',(⍕status),', expected 400'
      r,←(~'event-stream'Contains headers Header'content-type')Expect'a rejected request should not start a stream'
      (status headers body closed)←j Open'/events'
      r,←(status=200)Expect'accepted by ValidateRequestFn: status ',(⍕status),', expected 200'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_PostProcess;j;c
    ⍝ PostProcessFn is not called for SSE requests, but is for ordinary ones (the control) (plan §4.6)
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events'
      j.PostProcessFn←'AfterRequest'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start with PostProcessFn failed'
      {}j Open'/events'
      {}⎕DL 0.3
      r,←(0=App.PostCalled)Expect'PostProcessFn should not be called for an SSE request'
      c←j Echo ⍬
      {}j Read c'{}' 3000
      r,←(WaitFor'1=App.PostCalled' 2000)Expect'control: PostProcessFn was not called for an ordinary request'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Sessions;j;status;headers;body;closed
    ⍝ with sessions enabled, an SSE request gets a session like any other (plan §4.6)
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events'
      j.SessionTimeout←1
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start with SessionTimeout←1 failed'
      (status headers body closed)←j Open'/events'
      r,←((status=200)∧~closed)Expect'with sessions: status ',(⍕status),(closed/', stream closed')
      r,←(~0∊⍴headers Header j.SessionIdHeader)Expect'with sessions: no ',j.SessionIdHeader,' header in the SSE response'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_LastEventID;j;c
    ⍝ the endpoint function can read the Last-Event-ID header a reconnecting browser sends (plan §4.6)
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      c←j Request('GET' '/events'(('Accept' 'text/event-stream')('Last-Event-ID' '41')))
      {}j Read c(': connected',LF,LF)3000
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(1=≢App.Reqs)Expect'the endpoint function was not called'
      r,←((,'41')≡(⊃App.Reqs).GetHeader'last-event-id')Expect'req.GetHeader''last-event-id'' gave "',((⊃App.Reqs).GetHeader'last-event-id'),'"'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_HTTP10;j;c;data;closed
    ⍝ an HTTP/1.0 request gets an HTTP/1.0 close-delimited stream (plan §4.6)
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      c←j Request('GET' '/events'(,⊂'Accept' 'text/event-stream')'' 'HTTP/1.0')
      (data closed)←j Read c(': connected',LF,LF)3000
      r,←('HTTP/1.0 200'≡12↑data)Expect'HTTP/1.0: status line is ',Show data↑⍨¯1+⊃(⍸CRLF⍷data),≢data
      r,←(~closed)Expect'HTTP/1.0: stream closed'
      {}(j.SSEConnections'events')j.SendSSE'old'
      (data closed)←j Read c 1 2000
      r,←(('data: old',LF,LF)≡data)Expect'HTTP/1.0: event not received: ',Show data
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_NoCompression;j;c;status;headers;body;data;closed;enc
    ⍝ the stream is never compressed, even when compression is on and the client accepts gzip (plan §4.6)
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'events'
      j.UseZip←1
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      enc←⊂'Accept-Encoding' 'gzip'
      c←j Request('GET' '/events'((⊂'Accept' 'text/event-stream'),enc))
      (status headers body)←ParseResponse⊃j Read c(': connected',LF,LF)3000
      r,←(status=200)Expect'status ',⍕status
      r,←(0∊⍴headers Header'content-encoding')Expect'the SSE response has Content-Encoding: ',headers Header'content-encoding'
      r,←((': connected',LF,LF)≡body)Expect'the connected comment is not plain text: ',Show body
      {}(j.SSEConnections'events')j.SendSSE'plain'
      (data closed)←j Read c 1 2000
      r,←(('data: plain',LF,LF)≡data)Expect'event is not plain text: ',Show data
      c←j Echo enc
      (status headers body)←ParseResponse⊃j Read c(CRLF,CRLF)3000
      r,←((⊂headers Header'content-encoding')∊'gzip' 'deflate')Expect'control: an ordinary response was not compressed, so UseZip isn''t in effect'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_KillOnDisconnect;j;tid
    ⍝ a looping endpoint function stops after the client disconnects (plan §3 item 2):
    ⍝ killed at once with req.KillOnDisconnect←1, or when its next SendSSE fails with KillOnDisconnect←0
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'killme looper'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'

      {}j Open'/killme'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(WaitFor'0≠App.LoopTid' 2000)Expect'killme: the endpoint function did not start'
      tid←App.LoopTid
      {}j.LDRC.Close Last
      r,←(WaitFor('~',(⍕tid),'∊⎕TNUMS')3000)Expect'KillOnDisconnect←1: the endpoint thread was still running 3s after the client closed'
      ⎕TKILL tid

      App.LoopTid←0
      {}j Open'/looper'
      r,←(('data: tick',LF,LF)≡⊃j Read Last 1 2000)Expect'looper: no tick received'
      tid←App.LoopTid
      {}j.LDRC.Close Last
      r,←(WaitFor'1=App.LoopDone' 3000)Expect'KillOnDisconnect←0: the looping function did not stop within 3s of the client closing'
      ⎕TKILL tid
    ∇

:EndNamespace
